  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v3.2.8 (stable): Zero-copy browser download + service-worker seek-while-downloading + OPFS store perf. (1) Zero-copy web-seed download: a single-file torrent on a browser OPFS store keeps each piece's bytes in JS end to end (browser fetch -> Uint8Array -> SubtleCrypto 16 KiB-leaf hashes -> .NET Merkle tree over only the 32-byte hashes -> OPFS write); piece data never enters the .NET/WASM heap, per-piece verification preserved, desktop unaffected. (2) Multi-file zero-copy web seed (the SW streaming unlock; ~35x download vs the .NET block path on Sintel). (3) SW media streaming now supports seek-while-downloading on live torrents (the moov-never-arrived stall fixed via Critical()->UpdateWires debounce; plus _critical leak-on-cancel, last-piece stranding, and FIFO/idle-drain fixes). (4) OPFS AsyncFSChunkStore perf: last-whole-piece read cache (one OPFS read per piece instead of 16-64x re-reads), PutAsync via HeapView (one pinned memcpy instead of ToArray()+byte[] interop serialize; requires SpawnDev.BlazorJS 3.5.11), concurrent 16 KiB leaf hashing (Task.WhenAll). (5) O(pieces^2) picker fix on the zero-copy path: the budget check now runs inside the rarest/sequential walk loops so the walk stops the instant fetches are back in flight (was an O(pieces) re-scan per piece completion -> ~2.3MB/s on a ~1700-piece model); MaxWebConns 8->4 (at/under the browser ~6/origin HTTP/1.1 cap). (6) Web-seed download concurrency: fixed parallel range-request pipeline (MaxWebConns) instead of the chicken-and-egg speed-based pipeline that stayed at ~1 in flight. Requires SpawnDev.RTC 1.1.10 (periodic re-announce at the tracker interval, fixes cold-start swarm growth) + SpawnDev.BlazorJS 3.5.11. v3.2.7: Piece thread-safety (per-Piece re-entrant lock serializes the 8 state mutators; fixed a multi-threaded download race NRE on large torrents). v3.2.6: TorrentFileInfo.ReadUint8ArrayAsync zero-copy JS-typed range read.",
